  "full_text": "So if you've had a good day, you gotta have some bad times. So my newest approach is to, is boredom. It's kind of like, it's kind of, it like humbles you. You get grounded. You get very grounded when like you're just, you have nothing to do and you're like bored. If you feel worthless or, not worthless, but just very grounded. You know what I mean? Like, like. I'm doing nothing. Like your penance is like to do nothing, you know. You might, the reason I came up with a, the reason I suspect that's good is because in the past I would be high flying for a week of mania and then I would end up in a mental hospital for a week or a couple weeks. And so it seemed like, hey look, after a while I see a pattern. I have extreme excitement and intense and then i have extreme boredom and so and so i think it's good therapy to just be worthless because if you're worthless for a while then you got the flip side you know let's just say you overdo it you know church is basically boredom and it's uh it's basically magic to uh cause excitement so uh that's the way i look at it don't don't worry about me being bored because like i'm just basically you got your account of good and bad in your life and boredom is bad and anyway I'm in trouble",
